From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Prieto <simonepri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: fill flavors in order when splitting elastic scale-up

Elastic scale-up probes can leave free quota on an earlier flavor unused
when their whole count fits only on a later flavor. Rewriting Workload spec
from the scheduler would also race with the job reconciler.

Plan complete greedy fills without mutating scheduler inputs and
communicate their counts through the existing refusal note. The job
reconciler materializes the proposal through its resourceVersion-checked
split path. Quota accounting includes earlier PodSets, independent
resource groups, borrowing policy, lending limits, count steps and
reclaim floors. Workers need neither MinCount nor partial scale-up;
insufficient aggregate quota keeps the existing partial-admission
behavior.
---
